     "t": "code",
     "text": "====================================================================================================\nCHALKBOARD VISUAL LAYOUT \u2014 SLIDE 0003\n====================================================================================================\n[Plot: Sinusoidal Components of a Square Wave]\n\nPlot 1: Harmonic 1 (Fundamental)\n  T_{01} = 2 sec.  --->  \\omega_0 = \\pi rad/s\n  Single sinusoid completing 1 cycle in [0, 2 s]. Amplitude ~ 1.27 (4A/\\pi).\n\nPlot 2: Harmonic 3 (3rd Harmonic)\n  T_{02} = 2/3 sec.  --->  3\\omega_0\n  \\omega_{02} = 2\\pi / (2/3) = 3\\pi = 3\\omega_0\n  Sinusoid completing 3 cycles in [0, 2 s]. Amplitude ~ 0.42 (4A/3\\pi).\n\nPlot 3: Harmonic 5 (5th Harmonic)\n  T_{03} = 2/5 sec.  --->  5\\omega_0\n  Sinusoid completing 5 cycles in [0, 2 s]. Amplitude ~ 0.25 (4A/5\\pi).\n\nPlot 4: Harmonic 7 (7th Harmonic)\n  T_{04} = 2/7 sec.  --->  7\\omega_0\n  Sinusoid completing 7 cycles in [0, 2 s]. Amplitude ~ 0.18 (4A/7\\pi).\n\nPlot 5: Harmonic 9 (9th Harmonic)\n  T_{05} = 2/9 sec.  --->  9\\omega_0\n  Sinusoid completing 9 cycles in [0, 2 s]. Amplitude ~ 0.14 (4A/9\\pi).\n\nBottom Annotation:\n  - - -  \\infty  (Summing infinite odd harmonics synthesizes the square wave)\n===================================================================================================="
