      "7th Harmonic: $T_{04} = \\frac{2}{7}\\text{ s} \\implies \\omega_{04} = 7\\pi = 7\\omega_0$",
      "9th Harmonic: $T_{05} = \\frac{2}{9}\\text{ s} \\implies \\omega_{05} = 9\\pi = 9\\omega_0$",
      "**Convergence Behavior:** As the number of included harmonics increases, the sinusoidal ripple frequency increases, and the waveform flattens out in the constant regions, converging to the square wave everywhere except near discontinuities (Gibbs Phenomenon)."
